/E (A discipleship relationship that does not center on the Word of God is simply a friendship. This is the space in the discipleship meeting to use this discipleship binder! Review the tool together and make any notes here. Before you meet together, consider: Why is this tool important for the person you are discipling? What do you want them to take away from your time together? What questions can you ask to engage their head \(knowledge\), heart \(emotions\), and hands \(actions\)? Would it be more helpful based on our context to share this tool from memory, or simply read through it together?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
