/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Pastor and teacher John Mark Comer once remarked that our lives can feel like water in a pitcher, sloshing around when moved. Once the pitcher is placed steady on a table it will take the water some time to settle. This is often true of our lives in an ever more hurried culture. )
/Pg 56 0 R
/K [13]
>>
