/E (RHYTHMS: While this practice may be particularly helpful when facing an important decision, it is helpful to develop this discipline as a regular rhythm in our lives! Consider blocking out time weekly or monthly. Many have found it helpful to spend a weekend away with the Lord annually. Consider fasting during this time to remember how the Lord sustains you!)
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
2034 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3469 0 R
/E (DISTRACTIONS: It is only natural for distractions to arise! Keep a piece of paper close by to write down any tasks that come to mind that you might need to attend to later. Resist the temptation to work on something that comes up. Write it down and move on, knowing you can address it later. Consider silencing or even turning off your phone and electronics for this time.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
2035 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3470 0 R
/E (WHAT TO TAKE: Consider bringing noise canceling headphones, a pen and your journal, your Bible, any sermon or workshop notes you would like to review, verses you have been memorizing or meditating on, and possibly a devotional book. It may be helpful to bring old journals to review during this time.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
2036 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3471 0 R
/E (STAY ALERT: Be sure to get a good night sleep before setting out on this time. If spending all day or multiple days with the Lord, take breaks every so often to go for a walk, or go somewhere you can talk out loud. Give variety in what you do -- pray, journal, spend time in Scripture, etc.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
