/T (Aspen trees are unique in that they have roots that are connected together to unite the trees into one organism. So it is meant to be in the body of Christ -- we are designed to be interconnected to others in the body, united under the headship of Christ. As we journey through life, our primary source of fellowship may shift. In life, we may find belonging in places like friends, our church body, family, and/or marriage. In each of us is the danger towards extremes, either of isolation or co-dependence. Which extreme do you find it easiest to gravitate towards and why?)
